.TH GREEN-ROOMZ 1 "2026-09-03" "Green-Roomz 0.1.0" "Operator Manual"
.SH NAME
green-roomz \- local multimodal agent gateway
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B green-roomz
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.P
.B node bin/green-roomz.mjs
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Green-Roomz is a local, OpenAI-compatible agent gateway. It maps stable
functional aliases to host-qualified inference backends. It is llama.cpp-first
and runtime-agnostic. The only client-facing listener is
.B 127.0.0.1:8080
by default. The resident CPU nexus
.RB ( tool-router-agent )
listens on
.B :8187
and is pre-warmed at serve start.
.P
Cognitive agents compile the memory-feedback-loop frame. Treat what they know
as six states (derivation, attention, integration, partition, containment,
disintegration). The on-mind cache is L0 (DRAM-like B+tree index into the user
repository), L1 (near reminders), L2 (slower reminders / integrated store), and
L3 (will / identity last-level on-mind cache).
.P
.B 70% fill is L0+L1+L2+L3 COMBINED,
not L0 alone. Occupancy is an operator fact. Prefer
.I data/operator-usage.json
.RB ( /usage ).
If that file is absent, fill is unknown. Never invent occupancy numbers.
.P
Do not stop a live serve on :8080/:8187 from a docs-only session. Do not use
Windows
.B stop.cmd
against a Linux cursor serve.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B validate [--manifest path]
Inspect the manifest and print JSON (digest, degraded aliases, agent list).
Missing model files are reported unavailable; they do not invalidate the registry.
.TP
.B compile [--manifest path] [--check]
Write layered stock system prompts to
.IR build/prompts/ .
.B --check
exits non-zero if committed artifacts are stale.
.TP
.B prime [--manifest path] [--only a,b]
Snapshot each primeable agent's stock-prompt KV as
.BR default .
Needs
.I gateway.checkpoint_dir
or
.BR GREEN_ROOMZ_CHECKPOINT_DIR .
.TP
.B serve [--manifest path] [--host address] [--port number] [--allow-peer ip]
Listen. Default host/port come from the manifest (commonly 127.0.0.1:8080).
Attaches the operator TTY and appends to
.IR data/serve.log .
Pre-warms the nexus on :8187 when the artifact is present.
.TP
.B deploy [--manifest path] [--host address] [--port number] [--quick] [--prime]
Qualify missing agents, compile prompts, optionally prime, then serve.
.TP
.B benchmark [alias|all] [--manifest path] [--quick] [--force]
Qualify profiles. Results are cached by host fingerprint and artifact identity.
.TP
.B fingerprint [--manifest path]
Print the host fingerprint JSON.
.TP
.B doctor [--manifest path]
Validate plus fingerprint.
.TP
.B agents [--manifest path]
List models as JSON.
.TP
.B council-stats [task] [--json]
Read the council scorecard if
.I gateway.council_dir
is set.
.TP
.B stop [--manifest path]
Drain owned backends for this local process. Does not kill unrelated listeners.
.TP
.B help
Print command summary.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --manifest " path"
Agent manifest. Defaults to the host-appropriate file under
.I config/
(commonly
.I config/agents.windows.json
or, in the portable pack,
.IR config/agents.cursor.json ).
.TP
.BI --host " address"
Bind address for
.BR serve / deploy .
.TP
.BI --port " number"
Bind port for
.BR serve / deploy
(default 8080).
.TP
.BI --allow-peer " ip"
Repeatable. Trust one additional LAN IP. Non-loopback clients not listed get 403.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GREEN_ROOMZ_API_KEY
If set, require bearer authentication.
.TP
.B GREEN_ROOMZ_ALLOW_PUBLIC
Must be
.B 1
to bind a public address, and only together with an API key.
.TP
.B GREEN_ROOMZ_ANDROID_SIDECAR
Android sidecar endpoint; selects the Android host adapter.
.TP
.B GREEN_ROOMZ_ANDROID_TOKEN
Sidecar token (not logged, not copied into identity snapshots).
.TP
.B GREEN_ROOMZ_CHECKPOINT_DIR
Prime / restore directory if the manifest does not set
.IR gateway.checkpoint_dir .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config/agents.*.json
Host-qualified manifests (windows, android, note9, cursor).
.TP
.I policies/frames/memory-feedback-loop.md
Locked six-state / L0-L3 / 70% combined protocol.
.TP
.I data/operator-usage.json
Operator
.B /usage
drop-in. Schema: source, prompt_tokens, completion_tokens, total_tokens,
context_fill_pct (combined L0-L3 percent or null), notes. Install refresh must
not overwrite
.IR data/ .
.TP
.I data/operator-usage.example.json
Empty schema. Copy, then fill measured numbers. Do not pack a fake filled file.
.TP
.I data/serve.log
Serve console tee.
.TP
.I docs/strong-mind-will.md
Operator protocol (stutter, fugue, dream-then-compact, refusal/will).
.TP
.I docs/help/index.html
Self-contained dark-slate HTML help (Windows:
.IR help\\index.html ).
.SH OCCUPANCY
.B context_fill_pct
is total cache fill
.B L0+L1+L2+L3 combined.
The 70% hold is that combined cache. L3 is will/identity last-level on-mind
cache. Compaction of L0-L2 must not evict L3 without the user. Dream before
compact. Never compact undreamed items. Never invent fill.
.SH HTTP
Loopback routes include
.BR /health ,
.BR /v1/health ,
.BR /v1/models ,
.BR /v1/chat/completions ,
.BR /v1/embeddings ,
.BR /v1/rerank ,
.BR /v1/monitor/recent ,
.BR /metrics ,
.BR /props .
.P
.B POST /lockdown
and
.B POST /reboot
are not HTTP routes in this beta (404).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR grz-console (1),
.IR docs/strong-mind-will.md ,
.IR docs/diagrams/memory-stack.md ,
.IR docs/diagrams/serve-topology.md ,
.IR docs/diagrams/install-platforms.md ,
.IR docs/deployment.md ,
.IR docs/security-monitor-requirements.md ,
.IR docs/note9-termux.md
.SH BUGS
Health
.B degraded
is normal when specialist artifacts are missing. Default llama profile is
cpu-4 (4 threads). Do not leave 8 threads resident on the 0.5B nexus.
